      "hints": [
        "For $x > 2$, the term $x - 2 > 0$, so $\\frac{3}{x-2} > 0$.",
        "As $x \\to 2^+$, $\\frac{3}{x-2} \\to \\infty$, and as $x \\to \\infty$, $\\frac{3}{x-2} \\to 0$.",
        "State the range of $f(x)$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Analyze the behaviour of $f(x) = 1 + \\frac{3}{x - 2}$ on the domain $x > 2$:\n$$\\text{For } x > 2, \\quad x - 2 > 0 \\implies \\frac{3}{x - 2} > 0$$\n$$\\lim_{x \\to 2^+} f(x) = +\\infty, \\qquad \\lim_{x \\to \\infty} f(x) = 1$$",
        "State the range of $f$:\n$$f(x) > 1 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad y > 1 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad (1, \\infty)$$"
      ],
