      "hints": [
        "Set $y = 1 + \\frac{3}{x-2}$.",
        "Subtract $1$ and isolate $x-2$: $y - 1 = \\frac{3}{x-2} \\implies x - 2 = \\frac{3}{y-1}$.",
        "Solve for $x = 2 + \\frac{3}{y-1}$ and write $f^{-1}(x)$.",
        "The domain of $f^{-1}$ is the range of $f$ from part (a)."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set $y = f(x)$ and rearrange to make $x$ the subject:\n$$y = 1 + \\frac{3}{x - 2} \\implies y - 1 = \\frac{3}{x - 2}$$",
        "Clear fractions and solve for $x$:\n$$x - 2 = \\frac{3}{y - 1} \\implies x = 2 + \\frac{3}{y - 1} = \\frac{2(y - 1) + 3}{y - 1} = \\frac{2y + 1}{y - 1}$$",
        "Interchange variables to express $f^{-1}(x)$ and state its domain:\n$$f^{-1}(x) = 2 + \\frac{3}{x - 1} \\quad \\left(\\text{or } \\frac{2x + 1}{x - 1}\\right)$$\n$$\\text{Domain of } f^{-1}: \\quad x > 1$$"
      ],
